--- !u!114 &1198637797
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1198637795}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'THE GREAT STUFFED-GOAT HEIST

    Two teams of three trucks contest one
    oversized, non-gory stuffed sheep. Five minutes, most deliveries wins; a tie
    continues in sudden death. Up to four local humans, editable individual/team
    names, independent sources and AI difficulty. Blue owns the near corral; orange
    the far one.


    MOVE drives, steers, brakes then reverses. ACTION near loose
    cargo with clear line of sight attaches a physical tow rope. ACTION again releases
    it. One owner, no teleport. Cargo mass affects acceleration and turns; the rope
    stretches within a bounded length and force and can break. It cannot pass through
    barriers.


    DEFEND OR ESCORT

    A meaningful opposing truck contact into
    the carrier breaks its rope, using actual incoming normal speed above4.5m/s.
    Friendly bumps and cosmetic/trigger contacts do not break it. A0.8s protection/debounce
    separates attach/break events. Teammates escort, screen and defend; AI uses the
    same action eligibility and physical motors.


    DELIVER THE WHOLE CARGO

    The
    entire cargo scoring box must enter YOUR painted corral while a live teammate
    owns its rope. Truck entry alone or an unowned sheep earns nothing. Each delivery
    locks once, celebrates, then resets both teams and cargo fairly. Five-minute
    clock pauses during celebrations/recovery. Unreachable fallen cargo resets neutrally
    after1.5s; immobile unattended cargo resets after12s without an approach. A cargo
    body genuinely pressed against a solid lateral wall with less than0.65m progress
    for18s triggers an announced neutral recovery; ordinary open-field crowding does
    not. A stationary upside-down truck for5s or real out-of-bounds fall receives
    the same1.5s announced return to an unoccupied home grid for humans and AI; no
    forward warp or scoring advantage. Score/clock persist.


    Shared elevated
    broadcast frames both goals and all six trucks. Pause/disconnect preserves bodies,
    rope, score and clock. Reconnect or explicitly replace, release controls and
    freshly confirm. Rematch retains names and source setup. Offline only.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be1034cebd9fa3643a48d11ef76e4708, type: 2}
